 "overview": {
  "summary": "The high voltage half of the calibrator, and one of a pair -- A14 does not work without A15 and A15 does not work without A14. A14 carries transformer T1 and the sixteen relays that reconfigure it, so it is the board that turns the Power Amplifier's output into the 1100 V ac range, the +/-1100 V dc range and the 2.2 A range. It rectifies and filters those into +/-HVDC across C1 and into the VI+ / VI- pair for the current range. It measures its own output through a peak detector. And it carries the magnitude control loop that regulates all of it, plus the 82C55 and four driver ICs that operate every relay and control line on both assemblies. A17 and A18 are supplies that either work or do not; A14 is a servo, and most of its failures are the loop misbehaving rather than a part being dead.",
  "sections": "§2-155 … §2-167",
  "note": "The board is exposed on the extender card with the rear shield (MP3) removed, and it carries the 1100 V range output, +/-HVDC across C1 and the T1 secondary. C1 is 0.72 uF: charged to 1100 V it holds about 0.44 J, and with the 600 kilohm bleeder of R3-R5 the time constant is roughly 0.4 s. It does discharge, but confirm it before working near it."
 },
