    "note": "The regulator that sets the amplitude of HVCL and therefore the level of every high-voltage and high-current supply. Five blocks: the absolute value circuit (U2A/U2B, Q3, CR8, CR9) forms the dc equivalent of G OUT's positive peaks; signal/polarity selection (U2C, U6) subtracts the supply from it to make ERROR SIGNAL; the reference and error amplifier (U2D with C18 as integrator, U7B, Q4, VR1) balances that against a reference which changes with function -- 6.8 V in the HV dc range, 3.1 V in the 2 A dc range, 5.2 V in the 2 A ac function -- and produces AMPLITUDE; U4 generates the 1 kHz QSQB; and U3 switches between +AMPLITUDE and -AMPLITUDE through U7C/U7D and amplifies by 2.6 to make HVCL. PS OFF turns on Q2 to short C18 and force AMPLITUDE to zero until A15 is set up.",
