   "nominal": 227,
   "tolerance": 1,
   "unit": "V",
   "hazard": "HIGH VOLTAGE",
   "condition": "+220 V dc, operate. Measured across the capacitor, not to PACOM.",
   "source": "§5-19 step 6 (step 6)",
   "note": "C1 filters the rectified transformer output into +/-HVDC, and R3-R5 form a 600 kilohm bleeder across it. A reading much greater than 227 V is a magnitude control fault, not a filter fault, and sends you to §5-20 -- step 6 says 'starting at step 10', which in this numbering is the square wave generator check. No dc at all points at the transformer, its range relays or the bridge.",
