   "condition": "Power-up transient. Scope at 5 V/div, connected before power-up.",
   "source": "§5-20 step 3 (step 12)",
   "note": "The mirror of the CR10 check: this should ramp down to approximately -14 V, hold about a second and return to 0 V. U1A inverts AMPLITUDE so the square wave amplifier can swing between +AMPLITUDE and -AMPLITUDE. If this is right and TP3 is still dead at power-up, the fault is downstream in U3 or the U7 switches.",
