   "source": "§5-20 step 4 (step 13)",
   "note": "Checked against G OUT rather than against a number: note the amplitude of the positive wave peaks at G OUT, then verify the dc voltage here equals them. U2A generates a negative half-wave equal to those peaks and U2B sums and averages it, so in the high-voltage dc function -- where the 2.2 A amplifier is unused -- this output is 0 V and that is correct. Remove the jumper before continuing.",
